From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Son Luong Ngoc <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:37:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj: Delegate narrow prefix disambiguation

Short ID formatting currently materializes every commit/change pair in
its configured disambiguation revset. A remote index can answer the same
prefix questions without transferring unrendered canonical history.

Let a revset optionally return an owned exact prefix provider. Cache it
in the existing context, and retain materialization when no provider is
available. Keep global fallback, current-view membership and change
visibility checks, and bookmark/tag name precedence on the client.

The default hook returns None. Providers must preserve the complete
selection or decline delegation; filtered streams and canonical object
access are not changed. Independent I/O ownership is required because
existing synchronous prefix calls may block their caller's executor.

